2	//
3	// JavaScript's primitive types lose distinctions that PyYAML keeps after
4	// resolving a scalar (int vs float, string vs timestamp). The loader wraps
5	// those scalars in the classes below so the dumper can reproduce PyYAML's
6	// exact output.
7	//
8	// Value model produced by safeLoad() and consumed by safeDump():
9	//   - string        -> YAML str
10	//   - number (int)  -> YAML int
11	//   - boolean       -> YAML bool
12	//   - null          -> YAML null
13	//   - Array         -> YAML sequence
14	//   - plain Object  -> YAML mapping (keys are strings)
15	//   - YFloat        -> YAML float
16	//   - YTimestamp    -> YAML timestamp (date / datetime)
